owing steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}]}], "template_override": 1}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "John in Brazil"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Bright Future"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Nature Around Us > Rainforest"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making and Responding to Suggestions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Making Suggestions</span><br>  <br>You use modals when you want to give suggestions. </br><span class=\"strong\">Might</span> is often used with <span class=\"strong\">want</span> to give suggestions.<br>  <br>Example:<br>  <br><span class=\"italic\">You might want to look at the ingredients in your shampoo.<br> You might want to grab your umbrella.</span><br>   <br>You can use the word, <span class=\"strong\">Let's </span> with a verb to make a suggestion.<br> Let's is the short form of Let us. <br>  <br>Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\"> Let's go to the park. The weather is great!<br></span>  <br>You can also use Wh- questions:<br>  <br>Why don't you \u2026 ?<br>  How about \u2026 ?<br>  <br>Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\">Why don't you study at the library?<br> How about studying at the park?<br></span>   <span class=\"strong\"><br>Responding to Suggestions<br></span>  <br>You can accept suggestions by saying:<br>  <span class=\"italic\"><br>Yes, I'd like to.<br> Yes, I'd love to.<br> What a good idea!<br> Why not?<br></span>   <br>You can refuse suggestions by saying:<br> <br><span class=\"italic\">No, let's not.<br> No, I'd rather not.<br> I don't feel like it.<br></span>"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Cause and Effect"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use expressions like  <span class=\"italic\">because</span>, <span class=\"italic\">since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">owing to</span>, and  <span class=\"italic\">due to</span> to talk about the results of  a certain cause.<br>   <br><span class=\"strong\">Example:</span> <span class=\"italic\"><br>We went for a jog in the park  <span class=\"strong\">because</span> it was such a nice day.<br> The doctor refused to discharge the patient  <span class=\"strong\">since</span> his test results were unclear.<br> She can't read the letter <span class=\"strong\">as</span> she is not fluent in Mandarin.<br> He can't join the group <span class=\"strong\">for</span> he has an appointment.<br> <span class=\"strong\">Owing to</span> his knowledge of weather patterns, he knew rain was coming.<br> <span class=\"strong\">Due to</span> the bad weather, they didn't go on the hiking trip.<br> </span>  <br>You can also say:<br> <ul><li>The cause of \u2026 is \u2026</li> <li>\u2026 is caused by / is due to \u2026</li> <li>Thanks to ...</li></ul><br>  <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br>  <br>The cause of global warming is pollution.<br> Global warming is caused by/is due to pollution.<br> Thanks to global warming, the seas are rising.<br>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "impact "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a powerful or major influence or effect "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Cutting down the trees had a negative impact on the community."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to  talk about ecological issues."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deforestation  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cutting down or burning all the trees in an area"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is a lot deforestation happening in the world."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "way of life "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a typical way in which a person or group lives "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They had to change their way of life."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "public"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the people of a country "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We decided to create our own products and sell them to the public."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chemical"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a substance that is made by a chemical process"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are chemicals in our food."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "artificial"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not natural or real "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are no artificial ingredients in the soap."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "warehouse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large building used for storing goods "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The products are stored in the warehouse."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shipment"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a load of goods sent to a customer or store "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are sending out a big shipment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob08aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to carry"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have something ready to be sold "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How many products do you carry?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob08aud09"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le06ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Use your imagination, and write complete sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your answers with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the sentences aloud."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Cause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Positive Effect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative Effect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Because the smell of the shampoo was very strong ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Because John missed the tour bus in Costa Rica ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Because Vanessa went for a long walk on the beach in Mexico ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Because Peter went out for dinner with friend from work ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write sentences using cause and effect to describe situations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice speaking by saying the sentences to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use my imagination to talk about situations in other countries."}]}], "type": "sena"}